module v4.extdeps.languages.typescript


// `Bool` is kernel-ambient (STRUCTURE.md:147). `type TsBoolean = Bool`
// references std/logic.dag's `Bool` without an `import` — correct alias-
// identity, not hollow.


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (D2 slice)
//
// ECMAScript partitions `number` (IEEE-754 binary64) and `bigint`
// (exact integers, unbounded) as DISTINCT primitives — not Rust's `i32`
// fixed-width ladder. Structural typing, excess property checks, and
// conditional types are **out of D2** (DECISIONS.md D2 scope guard).


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// D2a(2) — GROUNDING MAP (🟡 ENTIRE FACET DEFERRED — operator-pending)
//
// Per mgr brief msg_6d3a3eb2: `GroundingMap` is SHARED with no pinned P2
// home yet. Declaring a local `GroundingMap` in each language file would
// be N parallel declarations — forbidden. **Defer** the carrier type AND
// every `data ts_*_grounding` instance row until the operator pins the
// shared `GroundingMap` authority (escalation path). Includes deferred
// `boolean` / `number` / `bigint` keyword grounding data.


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Primitive vocabulary — ECMAScript numeric surface (Handbook + ECMA-262)
//
// TypeScript inherits ECMAScript's two numeric primitives: `number` and
// `bigint` (distinct from Rust's signed/unsigned fixed-width family).
//
// Spec: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html
//       (sections on `number`, `bigint`)
//       https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-ecmascript-language-types-number-type
//       https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-ecmascript-language-types-bigint-type
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: both kinds are shared classifiers for every
//      consumer that dispatches on numeric primitive kind.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: nullary tags from a closed ECMA-262
//      partition; a `Bool` proxy would be the M4 numeric/boolean-proxy smell.
//   3. Algebraic form — PARTIAL: each kind's algebra is std/ (float vs
//      integer chains) reached via **future** D2a(1) aliases, not by
//      collapsing this enum into those carriers.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a value is exactly ONE numeric primitive kind.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: `number` and `bigint` are distinct
//      ECMA primitives, not one indexed family (Practice 7).
type TsEcma262NumericPrimitiveKind
  = TsNumberPrimitive
  | TsBigIntPrimitive


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// D2a(1) — alias-identity (kernel-ambient `Bool`)


// ECMAScript / TypeScript `boolean` ↔ std/logic.dag `Bool`.
// Spec: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html
//       https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-ecmascript-language-types-boolean-type
type TsBoolean = Bool


// D2a(3) — **omitted** for `boolean`: no ECMA-262 operation-semantics event
// distinct from `BooleanAlgebra<Bool>` (std/logic.dag); no parallel
// overflow / NaN carrier.


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// D2a(3) — ECMA-262 `Number` primitive semantics (NOT integer overflow)
//
// ECMA-262 defines two standard **axes** on the `Number` type value domain:
//   (A) Additive / multiplicative / division / remainder on Number values
//       follow IEEE-754 binary64 (including NaN / ±∞ propagation), not
//       two's-complement fixed-width wrap.
//   (B) Bitwise operators coerce via ToInt32 / ToUint32 — results are
//       integers mod 2³² in two's-complement / unsigned binary32 layout
//       per ECMA-262 — a **different** spec surface from (A).
//
// These are modeled as **two singleton carriers** (each N=1) so each axis
// carries its own 🟢 terminal Practice-4 ledger without falsely merging
// distinct spec obligations into one ambiguous coproduct value.
//
// Spec (A): https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-numeric-types-number-type
// Spec (B): https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-numberbitwiseop (Number::BitwiseOp)


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// TsNumberAdditiveMultiplicativeSemantics — axis (A).
//
// Coproduct dissolution — 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: shared by every additive/multiplicative
//      Number consumer uniformly.
//   2. Variant-is-data — N/A (N=1 exhaustive for this axis in ECMA-262).
//   3. Algebraic form — PARTIAL: IEEE-754 structure is std/float.dag +
//      `ApproximateField` (D2b); this tag names the ECMA **Number-type**
//      commitment to that axis, not the full float algebra body.
//   4. Dimensional — N/A (singleton).
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: not an indexed family over widths.
//
// N=1 note: ECMA-262 admits exactly one standard behavior class for (A) on
// `Number` values; a second variant would fabricate a distinction the spec
// does not own.
type TsNumberAdditiveMultiplicativeSemantics
  = Ieee754Binary64Ecma262NumberType


data ts_number_additive_multiplicative_semantics: TsNumberAdditiveMultiplicativeSemantics = Ieee754Binary64Ecma262NumberType


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// TsNumberBitwiseSemantics — axis (B).
//
// Coproduct dissolution — 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: shared by every bitwise Number consumer.
//   2. Variant-is-data — N/A (N=1 for this axis).
//   3. Algebraic form — PARTIAL: modular 2³² arithmetic is a finite ring
//      side-effect of ToInt32/ToUint32 coercion — the authoritative numeric
//      story remains IEEE-754 for non-bitwise Number ops; this tag isolates
//      the bitwise coercion track per ECMA-262.
//   4. Dimensional — N/A (singleton).
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: not parameterized over machine widths
//      at the TS language-primitive layer (`number` is not `i32`).
type TsNumberBitwiseSemantics
  = Int32Uint32ModuloTwoPow32Ecma262


data ts_number_bitwise_semantics: TsNumberBitwiseSemantics = Int32Uint32ModuloTwoPow32Ecma262


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// D2a(3) — ECMA-262 `BigInt` primitive semantics
//
// `bigint` is an exact, unbounded integer primitive — no Rust-style
// fixed-width overflow/wrap axis; invalid operations throw (e.g. division
// by zero) per ECMA-262, not silent modular wrap on a bounded width.
//
// Spec: https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-ecmascript-language-types-bigint-type
//       https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html
//
// Coproduct dissolution — 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: shared classifier for all BigInt consumers.
//   2. Variant-is-data — N/A (N=1 for the primitive's core semantics class).
//   3. Algebraic form — PARTIAL: exact integer algebra is std/integer.dag
//      (`Int` chain) reached via **future** D2a(1) alias — this tag names the
//      ECMA **BigInt-type** exact-unbounded commitment, not the `Int` body.
//   4. Dimensional — N/A (singleton).
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: not `BigInt<Width>`.
type TsBigIntPrimitiveSemantics
  = ExactUnboundedIntegerEcma262BigIntType


data ts_bigint_primitive_semantics: TsBigIntPrimitiveSemantics = ExactUnboundedIntegerEcma262BigIntType


